package toolruntime

const StatisticalEvidenceInstructions = ` Keep statistical explanations exact and limited to what was established. Arithmetic mean is sum/count and is sensitive to extreme values; never call it robust or insensitive to outliers. A histogram's count is an observation count, not seconds or the source's measurement unit; its sum and sum/count use the original measurement unit. A mean is not P95, a bucket boundary is not a measured percentile, and an unqueried percentile remains unknown. PromQL can numerically aggregate Gauge and Counter float series or different physical units; the engine does not automatically certify unit or business-semantic compatibility. Do not claim a blanket engine rejection when the real limitation is meaningless mixed-unit analysis. Do not add unsupported general statistical claims to an otherwise correct numeric summary. `
